      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Property Shop are delighted to present No. 16 Swords Street to the Stoneybatter market. This beautifully presented home has been cleverly designed to maximise both space and natural light, offering bright, contemporary accommodation throughout. The current owners have maintained the property to an exceptional standard, something that is immediately evident upon entering. No. 16 presents a fantastic opportunity to acquire a stylish and sophisticated modern home, beautifully complemented by the charm and character of a traditional cottage-style property.\r\nThe accommodation comprises a spacious open-plan living and dining room, a modern kitchen, full shower room and two double bedrooms. To the rear, the property benefits from an attractive east-facing patio yard, while on-street parking is available to the front.\r\nThe location is second to none. Swords Street is just moments from the heart of Stoneybatter, renowned for its vibrant community atmosphere and excellent selection of independent cafés, restaurants, bars and local shops. A host of everyday amenities are also close by, including supermarkets and a choice of primary and secondary schools. The beautiful Phoenix Park is also within easy walking distance.\r\nSmithfield Village, Phibsborough and Dublin City Centre are all readily accessible on foot, while the area is exceptionally well served by public transport. Dublin Bus services, the Luas and Heuston Station, with its extensive rail connections, are all within easy reach, making the property an ideal choice for those seeking convenient city living. With its blend of modern style, charming character and an enviable Stoneybatter location, No. 16 Swords Street is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers. Viewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment through our Manor Street office.\r\n\r\nLounge 6.37m (20'11\") x 3.22m (10'7\")\r\nEntering through the hall door to a light filled living room, with high ceilings, stove, ample room to relax and dine, wood flooring and shuttered window.\r\n\r\nKitchen 2m (6'7\") x 3.17m (10'5\")\r\nModern fitted kitchen with eye & floor level units, integrated appliances, tiled surround & continuation of wood flooring.  Access to the rear patio.\r\n\r\nShower Room 1.41m (4'8\") x 2m (6'7\")\r\nModern shower room with screened mains Rain Forest shower area, feature tiling, WHB & WC.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 3m (9'10\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\r\nA cosy double bedroom to the rear of the property, continuation of the wood flooring, built in wardrobe & shelving. Shuttered window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 3.11m (10'2\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\r\nA second double room to the front of the property with a Murphy built in bed, currently used as a home office. Wood flooring and shuttered window.\r\n\r\nExterior 3.9m (12'10\") x 2.06m (6'9\")\r\nPatio deck to the rear with room for a table & chairs, on street disc parking to the front.\r\n\r\nArea \r\nApprox. 46 Sq Mts / 495 Sq Mts"
      },
